Jaime has 64 eggs and 2 trays, each holding 24 eggs. The total capacity of the trays is calculated as follows:

$$
2 \text{ trays} \times 24 \text{ eggs/tray} = 48 \text{ eggs}
$$

Subtracting this from the total number of eggs:

$$
64 \text{ eggs} - 48 \text{ eggs} = 16 \text{ eggs}
$$

Thus, the number of eggs Jaime won't be able to place on the tray is **16**.

